---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "Rent vs Buy Rent Growth (How to set assumptions)";
const description =
  "How to choose rent growth assumptions for rent vs buy modeling, using local data and scenario ranges. Educational use only.";

const lastUpdated = "2026-02-08";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/guides/rent-vs-buy-rent-growth" lastUpdated={lastUpdated} robots="noindex, follow">
  <section class="card hero">
    <span class="pill">Guide</span>
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/guides">Guides</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">Rent growth</span>
    </nav>
    <h1>Rent growth assumptions for rent vs buy</h1>
    <p>
      Rent growth drives how fast the renting scenario costs rise. This guide shows how to set a realistic rent growth assumption and
      how to test a range of outcomes.
    </p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/rent-vs-buy-calculator">Rent vs buy calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/rent-vs-buy-break-even">Break-even guide</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/topics/rent-vs-buy">Rent vs buy topic hub</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Rent vs buy inputs to verify</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Holding period (time horizon).</li>
      <li>Mortgage rate, down payment, and closing/selling costs.</li>
      <li>Rent growth and home appreciation assumptions.</li>
      <li>Maintenance, taxes, insurance, HOA, and investment return.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Start with local data</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
      Use recent local rent comps and lease renewals if you have them. National averages can be misleading, especially in high-growth
      or stable markets.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Account for lease terms</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Short leases can reset to market rates faster.</li>
      <li>Long leases can lock in lower growth temporarily.</li>
      <li>Concessions should be reflected as lower effective rent.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Use a scenario range</h2>
    <ol class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Pick a conservative rent growth rate.</li>
      <li>Add a base case from recent local trends.</li>
      <li>Test a higher-growth scenario if your market is volatile.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Decision inputs</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Current rent and lease term length.</li>
      <li>Local rent growth range from recent years.</li>
      <li>Expected move timeline or neighborhood change.</li>
      <li>Concession adjustments that change effective rent.</li>
      <li>Budget cap for future rent increases.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Common mistakes</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Using a high growth rate without a conservative case.</li>
      <li>Assuming rent growth is flat in a rising market.</li>
      <li>Ignoring the effect of moving to a different neighborhood or unit type.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">FAQ</h2>
    <h3 style="margin:12px 0 0">Should rent growth match home appreciation?</h3>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:8px 0 0">
      Not necessarily. Rent growth and home appreciation can move differently based on local supply, demand, and income growth.
    </p>
    <h3 style="margin:12px 0 0">What if I plan to move to a cheaper area?</h3>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:8px 0 0">
      Use a lower rent baseline or a scenario that reflects that move. Keep assumptions consistent across scenarios you compare.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="grid" style="margin-top:18px">
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related tools</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/calculators/rent-vs-buy-calculator">Rent vs buy calculator</a></li>
        <li><a href="/calculators/mortgage-payment-calculator">Mortgage payment calculator</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related guides</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/guides/rent-vs-buy-home-appreciation">Home appreciation assumptions</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/rent-vs-buy-time-horizon">Time horizon impact</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/rent-vs-buy-checklist">Rent vs buy checklist</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Next steps</h2>
    <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:10px">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/rent-vs-buy-calculator">Run the calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/rent-vs-buy-break-even">Break-even guide</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/rent-vs-buy-checklist">Rent vs buy checklist</a>
    </div>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0">Educational use only. Not financial advice.</p>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0; font-size:13px">Last updated: 2026-02-08</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>



